# `lti::PoleZero`

A pole-zero-gain system.

## Signature

```cpp
const pluss::Series& lti::PoleZero::zeros() const noexcept;
const pluss::Series& lti::PoleZero::poles() const noexcept;
const pluss::Series& lti::PoleZero::gain() const noexcept;

double lti::PoleZero::sample_time() const noexcept;
bool lti::PoleZero::is_cont() const noexcept;
bool lti::PoleZero::is_disc() const noexcept;
bool lti::PoleZero::is_stable() const;
```

## Construction

Returned by `zpk` and the filter designs.

## Methods

| Method | What it does |
|---|---|
| [`zeros`](PoleZero/zeros.md) | The zeros of the transfer function. |
| [`poles`](PoleZero/poles.md) | The poles of the transfer function. |
| [`gain`](PoleZero/gain.md) | The scalar gain of the zero-pole-gain form. |
| [`sample_time`](PoleZero/sample_time.md) | The sample period in seconds; zero for a continuous-time system. |
| [`is_cont`](PoleZero/is_cont.md) | Whether the system is continuous-time (sample time zero). |
| [`is_disc`](PoleZero/is_disc.md) | Whether the system is discrete-time (sample time positive). |
| [`is_stable`](PoleZero/is_stable.md) | Whether every pole lies in the stable region for the system's time domain. |

## Changelog

- **0.1**: initial documented surface.

